-- title:
--   Total ramification of finite layers over a varpi-centred valuation ring
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, $A$ a valuation subring of $L$, and $C$ a subring of $L$ all of whose elements lie in $A$, such that $C$ is a domain and a discrete valuation ring. Let $\varpi \in C$ be an element with the properties: an element $d$ of $C$ has residue $0$ under the residue map of the local ring $A$ (applied to $d$ viewed in $A$) if and only if $d$ is a $C$-multiple of $\varpi$; the image of $\varpi$ in $L$ is non-zero; every element of $A$ differs from the image of some element of $C$ by an element of the maximal ideal of $A$; and $A$ is the unique valuation subring $V$ of $L$ which contains $C$ and in which $\varpi$ is a non-unit. Let $K_0$ be a field which is a fraction field of $C$ and a subfield of $L$ in a way compatible with the $C$-actions, and let $K_1$ be an intermediate field of $L/K_0$ that is finite-dimensional over $K_0$. Then there are elements $\varpi_1, v, w$ of $L$, all lying in $K_1$ and all integral over $C$, with $vw = 1$, $\varpi = v\,\varpi_1^{\,n}$ where $n = \operatorname{finrank}_{K_0} K_1$, and $K_0(\varpi_1) = K_1$.
--
--   This is the statement that, under the hypotheses that $\varpi$ generates the maximal ideal of $A$ relative to $C$, that $C$ surjects onto the residue field of $A$, and that $A$ is the only valuation ring of $L$ over $C$ at which $\varpi$ is not a unit, every finite layer $K_1/K_0$ inside $L$ is totally ramified, with a uniformiser $\varpi_1$ that generates $K_1$ and satisfies $\varpi = v\varpi_1^{[K_1:K_0]}$ for a unit $v$ integral over $C$ together with its inverse. It is used in the construction of annuli around a node, to bound the degree of the finite layer generated by a chosen uniformiser.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ValuationSubring_exists_eq_mul_pow_finrank_and_adjoin_simple_eq_of_forall_valuationSubring_eq.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
